{
  "requirement": "Each configurable feature MUST define the name and typed data structure of its\nuser section and any supported project section, citing these common configuration\nrequirements. The feature MUST specify its supported keys, value types, defaults,\nvalidation rules, and the precedence or combination rules for user settings,\nproject settings, and invocation options. It MUST specify the behavior of an\nabsent section and which operations require that section.\n\nFeature-specific fields MUST stay within the feature's section. A feature MUST\nNOT reinterpret another feature's settings or change the shared file locations\nor schema version. A feature MAY define a provider-owned options map, but MUST\ndocument that boundary and how those options are validated.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "I judge this requirement unsatisfied because nothing is marked as implementing or testing it.\n\n**What the reference index shows.** `requirements.configuration.feature_sections` has only two `{cite}` sites:\n- `md/requirements/authoring.md:486`, inside the `configuration` requirement.\n- `md/requirements/configuration.md:108`, inside `workspace_structure`.\n\nThere is no `{impl}` marker and no `{test}` marker anywhere. Under the assessment criteria, a `{cite}` alone does not count as implementation.\n\n**What the authoring feature does cover.** The authoring spec appears to meet much of the requirement in substance:\n- It defines `[authoring]` and its data structures in `configuration_structure`, with serialization rules in `configuration_serialization`.\n- It sets keys, types, defaults and validation in `configuration_storage` and `concurrency`.\n- It sets precedence in `configuration_precedence`.\n- It defines a provider-owned `options` map and says how it is validated.\n- It says what a missing configuration does: `resolve_authoring_with_workspace_from` in `src/config.rs` fails with a diagnostic when there is no authoring configuration.\n- It lets status and validation load the config without checking unused authoring settings.\n\nCode in `src/config.rs` carries `{impl}` markers for those authoring requirements, and `tests/configuration.rs` and `tests/authoring_cli.rs` carry the matching `{test}` markers.\n\n**The gaps.**\n1. No document or code is marked `{impl}` for `feature_sections`, so a reviewer cannot tell which sources are meant to satisfy its obligations.\n2. No test is marked `{test}` for the requirement. The cross-feature obligations are never checked:\n   - A feature must stay inside its own section.\n   - A feature must not change shared locations or the schema version.\n   - A feature must document its absent-section behavior and which operations require its section.\n3. The `[evidence]` feature is a second feature section. It is covered through `evidence_paths`, but it is not tied to `feature_sections` either.\n\nThe gaps are not acknowledged by any FIXME or issue reference, so FIXME does not apply.",
